[18.972268, "o", "> "]
[18.972365, "o", "   - File paths other than the required input file '\"'\"'/app/users.json'\"'\"' and output redirections should not appear in the args\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[18.972379, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[18.972449, "o", "   - The filter should be a single string containing the complete jq filter expression\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[18.972465, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[18.972715, "o", "**Note on examples below**: In the following Data Schema sections, all content following the '\"'\"'#'\"'\"' symbol is just explanatory commentary and will NOT appear in the actual JSON files. These comments are only provided to clarify the structure and requirements.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[18.972733, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[18.972821, "o", "**Input Data Schema**:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[18.972862, "o", "The input JSON file '\"'\"'/app/users.json'\"'\"' is an array of user objects with the following structure:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> [\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[18.972898, "o", "\u001b[?2004h>   {\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[18.972959, "o", "    \"id\": 1,                  # Unique numeric identifier for the user\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[18.972971, "o", "> "]
[18.973035, "o", "    \"username\": \"john_doe\",   # User'\"'\"'s unique username (string)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[18.973059, "o", "> "]
[18.973133, "o", "    \"email\": \"john@example.com\",  # User'\"'\"'s email address (string)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[18.973216, "o", "    \"status\": \"active\",       # User status: '\"'\"'active'\"'\"' or '\"'\"'inactive'\"'\"'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[18.973326, "o", "    \"last_login\": \"2024-10-02T20:59:10.109812Z\",  # ISO 8601 timestamp (UTC) of the last login\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[18.973401, "o", "    \"roles\": [\"admin\", \"editor\"]  # Array of roles assigned to the user (may be empty)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[18.973407, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[18.973414, "o", "  },\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[18.973498, "o", "\u001b[?2004h>   ...\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ]\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> **Output Data Schema**:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[18.973527, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[18.973635, "o", "The output JSON file '\"'\"'/app/active_users_report.json'\"'\"' must be an array of objects with the following structure:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> [\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[18.973704, "o", "  {\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[18.973746, "o", "    \"user_id\": 1,                 # Derived from '\"'\"'id'\"'\"' in input \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[18.973776, "o", "    \"username\": \"john_doe\",       # Retained from input \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[18.973834, "o", "    \"email\": \"john@example.com\",  # Retained from input \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[18.973872, "o", "> "]
[18.973938, "o", "    \"last_login\": \"2024-10-02\",   # Formatted from '\"'\"'last_login'\"'\"' in input\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[18.974017, "o", "    \"role_count\": 2,              # Count of '\"'\"'roles'\"'\"' from input\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[18.974094, "o", "    \"primary_role\": \"admin\"       # If '\"'\"'roles'\"'\"' is empty, this must be null (JSON null, not \"null\")\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[18.974133, "o", "  },\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[18.974154, "o", "  ...\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ]\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[18.974178, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> **Requirements**:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[18.974294, "o", "- You must use jq to perform this transformation. Using other programming languages (e.g., Python, Ruby) is strictly prohibited.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[18.974316, "o", "> "]
[18.974372, "o", "- Ensure that the output JSON is properly formatted with 2-space indentation.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[18.974392, "o", "> "]
[18.974466, "o", "- The output file must be created at the exact path '\"'\"'/app/active_users_report.json'\"'\"'.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[18.974754, "o", "- The jq command used to generate the output(along with the output redirection) must be saved to '\"'\"'/app/cmd.sh'\"'\"'. This file will be used to verify the correctness of your solution.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[18.974814, "o", "- The jq arguments and filter must be saved to '\"'\"'/app/jq_args.yaml'\"'\"' as specified in the instructions above.  '; tmux wait -S done\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[113.275294, "o", "\r\n**`/app/jq_args.yaml`**\r\n```yaml\r\nfilter: \"[.[] | select(.status == \\\"active\\\") | {user_id: .id, username: .username, email: .email, last_login: (.last_login | split(\\\"T\\\")[0]), role_count: (.roles | length), primary_role: (.roles[0] // null)}] | sort_by(.username)\"\r\nargs:\r\n  - \"--indent 2\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nNotes on the two design choices that matter for the graded reconstruction command:\r\n- Indentation is produced by the flag `--indent 2` (not `--tab`, and not the default 4-space pretty printer), so it lives in `args` as one string with its value.\r\n- `last_login` is formatted with `split(\"T\")[0]` rather than `strptime`/`strftime` because input timestamps carry fractional seconds (`2026-03-30T15:06:40.723617Z`), which jq's `fromdate` rejects.\r\n- `primary_role` uses `.roles[0] // null`, so 50 empty-role users get JSON `null`, not `\"null\"` or a missing key.\r\n\r\nGeneration and checks (run via `sh /app/cmd.sh` and an independent verifier at `/app/verify.sh`):\r\n\r\n```\r\nactive in input=346, rows in report=346\r\nok: keys are "]
[113.275392, "o", "user_id, username, email, last_login, role_count, primary_role\r\nok: fields match input (id/username/email/last_login/role_count/primary_role)\r\nok: sorted ascending by username\r\nok: file is 2-space indented jq output\r\nok: cmd.sh runs a jq command\r\nok: cmd.sh names input and output paths\r\ncmd.sh exit=0\r\nok: cmd.sh regenerates identical output\r\nok: jq_args.yaml has args\r\nok: jq_args.yaml has filter\r\nok: yaml has exactly keys: args, filter\r\nok: args is a list\r\nok: filter is a string\r\nok: args contain no file paths\r\nreconstruction exit=0\r\nok: yq-constructed command reproduces the report\r\n-----\r\nALL CHECKS PASSED   (verify_exit=0)\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe verifier cross-checks each row against the matching input record by `id` (status dropped, username/email retained, date-formatted login, role count, primary role or null), confirms the row set is exactly the 346 `active` users, and runs `jq $(yq -r '.args[]' ...) \"$(yq -r '.filter' ...)\" /app/users.json` byte-compared against the delivered report. `cmd.sh` also runs correctly "]
